{
 "problem": "Essential self-adjointness of chi(xi) + chi'(eta) for the Bullough-Dodd S-matrix",
 "nodes": {
  "S": {
   "text": "Known for every n: chi_n(xi) = n P_n A_1^2 P_n and chi'_n(eta) = n P_n B_n^2 P_n are each positive self-adjoint on H_n intersected with Dom(A_1^2), resp. Dom(B_n^2) (Theorem A_n), and AB is bounded (Tanimoto)",
   "side": "start",
   "depth": 0
  },
  "G": {
   "text": "Proven: the sum chi_n(xi) + chi'_n(eta) is self-adjoint on the intersection of their domains for every n, so (HA-T) holds for the Bullough-Dodd S-matrix at B = 1/2",
   "side": "goal",
   "depth": 0
  },
  "F1": {
   "text": "Try Kato-Rellich: show chi'_n(eta) is relatively bounded by chi_n(xi) with relative bound less than 1",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "S",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "F2": {
   "text": "Take the KLMN form sum of the two positive operators chi_n(xi) and chi'_n(eta)",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "S",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "F3": {
   "text": "Truncate one side: replace B_n^2 by the bounded operator min(B_n^2, M), so Z_A + Z_{B,M} is self-adjoint by bounded perturbation",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "S",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "F4": {
   "text": "Check whether chi_n(xi) and chi'_n(eta) strongly commute, so their sum is self-adjoint by joint spectral calculus",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "S",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "F5": {
   "text": "Apply Nelson's commutator theorem with a comparison operator such as the n-particle number or dilation generator",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "S",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "B1": {
   "text": "The sum T is a positive symmetric operator with Ran(T + 1) equal to all of H_n",
   "side": "bwd",
   "parent": "G",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "B2": {
   "text": "For every f in H_n there are u_M with (Z_A + Z_{B,M} + 1) u_M = f and bounds on ||Z_A u_M|| and ||Z_{B,M} u_M|| uniform in M",
   "side": "bwd",
   "parent": "G",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "B3": {
   "text": "The adjoint equation T* v = -v has only the solution v = 0",
   "side": "bwd",
   "parent": "G",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "B4": {
   "text": "The form sum of chi_n(xi) and chi'_n(eta) has operator domain equal to the intersection of their domains",
   "side": "bwd",
   "parent": "G",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "F6": {
   "text": "No relative bound exists: both are unbounded analytic shifts in opposite imaginary directions, so neither controls the other",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "F1",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "F7": {
   "text": "The form sum is a self-adjoint operator extending chi_n(xi) + chi'_n(eta) on the intersection domain",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "F2",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "F8": {
   "text": "Expand the cross term <Z_A u, Z_{B,M} u> over cosets of S_n: B acting on slots 2 to n commutes with A_1^2, giving a non-negative contribution",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "F3",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "F9": {
   "text": "Bound the same-slot cross term by c ||A_1 u|| ||min(B_n, sqrt M) u|| using that AB is bounded",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "F3",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "F10": {
   "text": "They do not commute: the S-symmetrisation P_n couples slot 1 to slot n",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "F4",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "B5": {
   "text": "A positive symmetric operator T with Ran(T + 1) = H is self-adjoint",
   "side": "bwd",
   "parent": "B1",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "B6": {
   "text": "Pass to weak limits as M goes to infinity: u_M converges to u in the domain with (T + 1) u = f",
   "side": "bwd",
   "parent": "B2",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "B7": {
   "text": "2 Re <Z_A u, Z_{B,M} u> is bounded below by -eps ||Z_A u||^2 - C ||u||^2, uniformly in M",
   "side": "bwd",
   "parent": "B2",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "B8": {
   "text": "Show the form sum's operator domain equals Dom chi_n(xi) intersected with Dom chi'_n(eta)",
   "side": "bwd",
   "parent": "B4",
   "depth": 2
  }
 },
